# Flutter Core Standards

You are a senior Flutter engineer writing production-grade, neat, maintainable code.

## Architecture (Clean Architecture — Strict)

Layers:
1. Presentation (UI + Provider)
2. Domain (Entities + UseCases + Repository Contracts)
3. Data (Models + DataSources + Repository Implementations)

- Dependency flow: Presentation → Domain → Data only
- Domain must be pure Dart (no Flutter imports)
- UI must NEVER access repositories or data sources directly
- All business logic goes through UseCases

Separation:
- UI → rendering only
- Provider → state + flow control
- UseCase → business logic
- Repository → abstraction
- DataSource → API / Firebase / local DB

Error flow: Data throws Exceptions → Domain converts to Failures → UI shows user-friendly messages

## State Management — Provider Only

- Use `provider` consistently (ChangeNotifier / ChangeNotifierProvider)
- Prefer `context.watch` for rebuilds, `context.read` for one-shot actions
- Prefer `Consumer` / `Selector` to limit rebuild scope
- No business logic inside widgets; call Provider methods / UseCases
- State in Provider only (except trivial local UI state: form controllers, toggles)
- Prefer immutable state objects; notifyListeners after state changes
- Do not mix Riverpod, Bloc, GetX, or other state solutions

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
final store = context.watch<ServicesStore>();
onPressed: () => context.read<ServicesStore>().addService(...);

// ❌ BAD — logic + repos in the widget
onPressed: () async { await FirebaseFirestore.instance... }
```

## Project Structure

- Feature-based folders when applicable
- Widgets must not contain business logic
- Keep files focused; split when responsibilities grow

## Theming & Tokens

- Colors from `AppColors` only — never `Colors.*` in widgets
- Spacing, radius, typography from centralized tokens
- Read theme via `Theme.of(context)` / `ColorScheme`
- Dark mode: preserve brand; only surface/background/contrast may differ
- Default `ThemeMode.system`

## Localization

- All user-facing text via l10n / easy_localization — no hardcoded UI strings
- Support RTL via theme/locale, not widget hacks

## Async, Feedback & Safety

- Handle every async error; UI must show loading / empty / error states
- Use centralized `ToastService` — never SnackBar / ScaffoldMessenger
- No hardcoded secrets; validate user input defensively

## Code Quality

- Prefer `StatelessWidget` + `const` where possible
- Prefer Flutter SDK over new packages unless justified
- No commented-out or dead code
- Generated code must compile and be production-ready
